chinaciv
========

The visual language and the map engine come from "usaciv" by Andrej Karpathy:

    usaciv — the United States as a strategy game
    Copyright (c) 2026 Andrej Karpathy
    https://karpathy.ai/usaciv/
    License: MIT

Used: the static-site engine under web/ (Canvas 2D renderer, procedural terrain / city / water art, camera,
hex grid, lens dock, city panel, almanac, share and export) and the web/data JSON contract.

Changes made in this repository: the China edition — Albers projection for China, hex grid and map frame,
province / city / county wiring, Simplified-Chinese interface and Almanac, 27 lens layers, science and culture
yields, pinyin search, self-hosted font subset, and the static deployment configuration.

Data
----

All figures come from public sources and keep their original licences: statistics communiqués of the National
Bureau of Statistics and provincial / municipal bureaus, the 7th National Population Census, UNESCO, Natural
Earth (public domain), OpenStreetMap (ODbL 1.0), USGS and NOAA (public domain), Global Energy Monitor (CC BY
4.0), WorldPop and ESA WorldCover (CC BY 4.0), IBTrACS, JRC, ACAG and Wikipedia (CC BY-SA 4.0). The site's
Almanac lists each publisher, licence, URL and year; the machine-readable list is web/data/sources.json.

Font: Noto Serif SC, subset and self-hosted, under the SIL Open Font License 1.1.
